// PhD Flopper (perk #9): hijacks the stock _zm_perk_electric_cherry pipeline (registered
// machine + stock nuke model) and presents it as PhD Flopper - fall/explosive immunity +
// slide-to-explode nova (purple Apothicon FX). No .csc - the stock cherry .csc owns the client side. docs/13_perks.md.
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_perk_phd_flopper.gsc
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_decontamination.gsc
// Per-round DEFCON room lockdown (stage 1: red alarm-light half). docs/37.
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_lockdown.gsc
// Lockdown CHALLENGE room (Phase A): trap -> 30 confined glitch zombies -> reward. docs/43.
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_lockdown_challenge.gsc
// Per-round random-3 access to the 9 Lab perk-alcove door gates.
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_perk_doors.gsc
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_coop_scaling.gsc
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_zombie_speed.gsc
// Bus Station cross-room trench: velocity-gated fall tax (PhD-negated). docs/03.
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_bus_trench.gsc
// Dual-switch power: BOTH Bus Station switches required (one each side of trench).
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_power.gsc
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_dev.gsc
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_perk_info.gsc
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_ui.gsc
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_health_bars.gsc
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_pap_levels.gsc
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_atmosphere.gsc
// Perk machine + Pack-a-Punch glow on power-on. Server (.gsc) sets a colour-index
// clientfield on the power_on flag; client (.csc, listed below by _acc_lui.csc) PlayFX's
// the glow. The .csc is the render half (server-side PlayFX does not render in this build).
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_perk_lights.gsc

// NSZ Brutus boss pack (custom aitype zm_brutus + BO2 model + custom anims).
// Assets imported via APE from model_export/_NSZ/_GDT/_NSZ_Brutus.gdt at the Mod
// Tools root; the script is vendored under scripts/_NSZ. Full audit:
// docs/research/NateSmithZombies_Brutus_BO2_boss_pack.txt
scriptparsetree,scripts/_NSZ/nsz_brutus.gsc

scriptbundle,brutus_bundle
xmodel,brutus_helmet
xmodel,bo2_brutus_fb_death
xmodel,perk_clip
fx,_NSZ/Brutus/spawn_fx
fx,_NSZ/Brutus/chest_fx
fx,_NSZ/Brutus/helmet_smoke
fx,fire/fx_fire_ground_rubble_50x50
// PhD Flopper slide/down explosion = the Apothicon Fury purple/void spawn-burst FX
// (stock dlc4/genesis .efx, source present in the Mod Tools - verified 2026-06-15).
// _acc_perk_phd_flopper.gsc #precaches + PlayFXs it; def_explosion is the fallback.
fx,dlc4/genesis/fx_apothicon_fury_spawn_in_exp

// Per-round DEFCON room lockdown red alarm lights (_acc_lockdown.gsc). Stock ZM
// .efx, source present in <tools>\share\raw\fx\light\ (verified 2026-06-15):
//   fx_light_flashing_red_factory_zmb = the Giant/factory flashing-red alarm light (primary)
//   fx_glow_blink_red_5               = softer blinking-red glow (acc_lockdown_use_glow 1)
fx,light/fx_light_flashing_red_factory_zmb
fx,light/fx_glow_blink_red_5

// Perk/PaP power-on glow FX (_acc_perk_lights.csc PlayFX's these client-side, one per perk
// colour). Recoloured clones of the proven green power-up aura, generated by
// tools/gen_perk_glow_fx.js into <tools>\share\raw\fx\acc\light\ (NOT in git - regenerate
// from that tool, like the external asset packs). The green source is confirmed to render
// in this build (validated in-game 2026-06-18).
fx,acc/light/fx_perk_glow_red
fx,acc/light/fx_perk_glow_green
fx,acc/light/fx_perk_glow_yellow
fx,acc/light/fx_perk_glow_orange
fx,acc/light/fx_perk_glow_amber
fx,acc/light/fx_perk_glow_blue
fx,acc/light/fx_perk_glow_white
fx,acc/light/fx_perk_glow_purple
fx,acc/light/fx_perk_glow_blacklight
fx,acc/light/fx_perk_glow_teal

// Charred Zombie base-horde reskin (Logical's Charred Zombie Pack): a custom
// aitype `archetype_charred_zombie` = stock factory-zombie behaviour/anims
// (zm_zombie.ai_bt + zm_factory_zombie anim tables) + charred character
// `c_zom_charred_zombie` (DLC3 sentinel body + DLC4 charred head) + matching
// `c_zom_charred_zombie_gib_def`. Character/gib materials pull transitively as
// MODEL dependencies, so they DODGE the brush-face shader trap (docs/29 §14) -
// same class of asset as the Brutus model, which builds fine here.
// Import: drag the pack's model_export/ + source_data/ into the Mod Tools root,
// then gdtdb /update (registers source_data/_charred_zombies.gdt).
// Whole-horde reskin = in Radiant, Remap the SINGLE base spawner
// (actor_spawner_zm_factory_zombie, origin -131.5 630.5 208) to the charred
// spawner class - do NOT duplicate it (a 2nd spawner => ~50/50 normal+charred mix).
// UNCOMMENT the line below AFTER the GDT is imported (else linker = "missing
// aitype"); the Radiant spawner placement also pulls the aitype as a BSP
// dependency, so this explicit line is belt-and-suspenders.
aitype,archetype_charred_zombie

// Stock "Giant" zombie BODY xmodel - used to SKIN the Glitch Stalker mini-boss so it stands out
// from the charred horde (_acc_boss_glitch.gsc SetModel). Stock base-game asset (t7_characters,
// gdtDB-registered, source bins on disk - NOT DLC/external); pulls its own materials transitively
// as a model dep (dodges the brush-face shader trap). Same 'base' skeleton + gib rig as charred,
// so the SetModel swap keeps anims/gibs intact. Verified via the glitch-base-skin workflow.
xmodel,c_zom_der_zombie_body1
// Stock "Giant" zombie HEAD xmodel - completes the FULL stock skin on the Glitch Stalker (the body
// above + this head; _acc_boss_glitch.gsc detaches the charred head and attaches this). Same stock
// der family + 'base' skeleton; links the same way as the body. (Use the gdtDB-registered name
// c_zom_der_zombie_head1 - the raw bin name c_zom_der_head_1 has NO xmodel GDT entry, so it fails
// to link. Same body/head naming family as c_zom_der_zombie_body1 above.)
xmodel,c_zom_der_zombie_head1

// Custom ground-pickup world models (referenced ONLY by SetModel in script, so
// the linker needs these explicit lines - same reason as the Glitch Stalker
// models above). Stock assets, gdtDB-registered (verified via the dropped-item
// model workflow); materials ride in transitively (dodge the brush-face trap).
//   p7_fxanim_zm_stal_ray_gun_ball_mod = Data Shard drop (_acc_data_shards.gsc)
// Boss Cyberware items - one distinct model each (_acc_boss_items build_item_pool).
// 5 props packed here; item 4 "Repair Kit" uses a runtime-loaded powerup icon (no
// line needed). (zombie_zapper_handle + p6_power_lever were tried and FAILED to
// link - "xmodel missing", not in ZM-common fastfiles - so they were swapped out.)
//   nitrous_tank=Gas Tank, octobomb=Li'l Arnie, teddybear=Teddy Bear,
//   rocket_shield=Rocket Shield, monkey_bomb=Monkey Bomb
xmodel,p7_fxanim_zm_stal_ray_gun_ball_mod
xmodel,p7_zm_zod_nitrous_tank
xmodel,p7_fxanim_zm_zod_octobomb_mod
xmodel,p7_boots_safehouse_01
xmodel,zombietron_gold_brick
xmodel,wpn_t7_zmb_zod_rocket_shield_world
xmodel,wpn_t7_zmb_monkey_bomb_world
// Plaza Implant Bench prop: Cyber City white metal workbench (stock t7_props, on
// disk at model_export/t7_props/p7_cai_work_table_metal_set/). NOT in zm_levelcommon,
// so the linker compiles it from its GDT and packs it here (needs gdtdb-registered).
xmodel,p7_cai_work_table_metal_03_white
// Underground "Foundry" props (stock t7 props; same p7_cai_ family as the workbench
// above, so they compile from their GDTs + pack here). Glitch Altar base = interactive
// kiosk; Data Cache = cargo crate; Overclock terminal = ticket kiosk. Verified vs the
// build ERRORLOG (the oracle - see stock-pickup-model-safety).
xmodel,p7_cai_sign_inteactive_kiosk
xmodel,p7_cai_stacking_cargo_crate
xmodel,p7_cai_ticket_kiosk_theatre

// Cymbal Monkey (cymbal_monkey_zm) + Octobomb / Li'l Arnie (octobomb_zm) are
// granted by boss items. Both weapon DEFS already ship in zm_levelcommon (every
// usermap loads it at runtime - assetlist lines 6175 + 6225), so we do NOT add a
// `weapon,<name>_zm` line here: that forces a re-pack from a GDT source that ISN'T
// on disk and errors "Unable to load weapon". Inclusion is done purely via CSV rows
// in gamedata/weapons/zm/zm_levelcommon_weapons.csv (is_weapon_included -> true);
// GetWeapon("octobomb"/"cymbal_monkey") then resolves from zm_levelcommon. (Earlier
// build error was self-inflicted by the redundant weapon, lines - removed.)

// LUI client pipeline foundation (server module + client mirror + Lua overlay).
// docs/28_lui_pipeline.md. The .lua is a rawfile (copied verbatim, parsed by the
// game's Lua VM at runtime - a Lua syntax error shows at load, NOT at link).
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_lui.gsc
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_lui.csc
// Client half of the perk/PaP power-on glow (REGISTER_SYSTEM mirror + PlayFX render).
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_perk_lights.csc
// Client half of the Phantom holographic glow aura (accPhantomAura clientfield -> PlayFXOnTag).
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_boss_phantom.csc
rawfile,ui/uieditor/menus/hud/acc_hud.lua

// Custom perk HUD icons (Ronan's Cyberpunk Shaders), drawn by acc_hud.lua's
// CoD.AccPerkBar via setImage(RegisterImage(...)). 2D UI `image` assets - NOT
// stock-name material overrides - so they take the docs/28 LUI image path and
// avoid the geometry-material shader-compile blocker (docs/29 §14). GDT =
// source_data/acc_perk_shaders.gdt (deploy: tools/deploy_perk_shaders.ps1).
// 9 live perks x base(red)/mega(teal); drives the perk row (acc_hud.lua bar-bit order).
image,i_acc_perk_jugg_base
image,i_acc_perk_jugg_mega
image,i_acc_perk_revive_base
image,i_acc_perk_revive_mega
image,i_acc_perk_speed_base
image,i_acc_perk_speed_mega
image,i_acc_perk_doubletap_base
image,i_acc_perk_doubletap_mega
image,i_acc_perk_staminup_base
image,i_acc_perk_staminup_mega
image,i_acc_perk_mule_base
image,i_acc_perk_mule_mega
image,i_acc_perk_deadshot_base
image,i_acc_perk_deadshot_mega
image,i_acc_perk_widows_base
image,i_acc_perk_widows_mega
// PhD Flopper (perk #9) - Ronan's Cyberpunk "exo_flopper" icon (base=Red variant,
// mega=root variant). GDT = source_data/acc_perk_shaders.gdt. Drives acc_hud.lua
// CoD.AccPerkBar bit 8. Credit Ronan + Treyarch per the pack readme.
image,i_acc_perk_phd_base
image,i_acc_perk_phd_mega

// Power-up HUD icons (Ronan's Cyberpunk Shaders): Insta-Kill / Double Points / Fire Sale.
// Drawn by acc_hud.lua CoD.AccPowerupBar while each power-up is active (accPowerupMask bits
// 0/1/2). GDT = source_data/acc_perk_shaders.gdt (deploy: tools/deploy_perk_shaders.ps1).
image,i_acc_powerup_instakill
image,i_acc_powerup_double
image,i_acc_powerup_sale
// Instant power-ups (Nuke / Max Ammo): no timed window, so acc_hud.lua flashes these for 3s on
// pickup (accPowerupMask bits 3/4, driven by _acc_lui pickup-flash watchers). Same Ronan art set.
image,i_acc_powerup_nuke
image,i_acc_powerup_maxammo
// Carpenter + Random Perk (free_perk bottle): also instant, flashed 3s on pickup via the generic
// powerup_dropped->powerup_grabbed watcher (bits 5/6). Drops may not be enabled on the map yet -
// the HUD wiring is in place for when they are.
image,i_acc_powerup_carpenter
image,i_acc_powerup_randomperk

// PaP tier roman-numeral icons (Ronan teal hex shields I/II/III). Drawn by acc_hud.lua
// CoD.AccPapTierIcon over the gadget HUD circle (bottom-right); driven by accPapTier (held
// weapon's current PaP tier 1..3, 0=hidden). GDT = source_data/acc_perk_shaders.gdt.
image,i_acc_pap_tier1
image,i_acc_pap_tier2
image,i_acc_pap_tier3

// (The stock perk bar is hidden by ZEROING its hudItems.perks.* uimodel fields in GSC -
// _acc_lui::clear_stock_perk_hud - NOT by asset override: a usermap zone loads LAST and a
// same-named base-zone asset always wins, so transparent image overrides do nothing.)

// Makes the linker read the weapons table (box needs this). The usermap copy
// at gamedata/weapons/zm/ (deployed by sync) overrides the stock table: it is
// the stock 50-weapon table + the 3 Skye box imports below.
stringtable,gamedata/weapons/zm/zm_levelcommon_weapons.csv

